From fa2e0c8a5d508029f4245ac75807fd0a25ae476a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ginux-watch-agent <actions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 12:16:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests(fs-policy): pin Rights constants to exact distinct bit
 positions
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

### What
Pins every `Rights` constant to its exact bit position (LOOKUP=1<<0 … EXECUTE=1<<5) and asserts pairwise non-containment so no two rights collapse onto the same bit.

### Why it matters
Capability checks are bitwise: shifting a constant right (`1 >> 3 == 0`) turns CREATE into the empty right that authorizes nothing, while colliding bits silently grant extra permissions. The existing `rights_contains_requires_every_requested_bit` test is shift-invariant (it only checks containment algebra), so it survives every `<<`->`>>` mutation.

### Mutation evidence (fail-then-pass)
| Mutant | Existing suite | New test |
|---|---|---|
| `CREATE: 1 << 3` -> `1 >> 3` | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |
| `METADATA: 1 << 4` -> `1 >> 4` | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |
| `EXECUTE: 1 << 5` -> `1 >> 5` | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |

Baseline (clean tree + new test): PASS. Reproduce: `cargo test -p ginux-fs-policy --lib rights_constants_pin_exact`.

Spec-Ref: capability rights bitmask contract (distinct single-bit rights)

Prepared with AI assistance; reviewed by me.
---
 crates/ginux-fs-policy/src/lib.rs | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/ginux-fs-policy/src/lib.rs b/crates/ginux-fs-policy/src/lib.rs
index 7bc7453d..9dfeac50 100644
--- a/crates/ginux-fs-policy/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/ginux-fs-policy/src/lib.rs
@@ -2373,4 +2373,30 @@ mod tests {
         // zero-hash fallback to 1 is preserved
         assert_ne!(identity_token(b""), 0);
     }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn rights_constants_pin_exact_bit_positions() {
+        assert_eq!(Rights::LOOKUP, Rights(1 << 0));
+        assert_eq!(Rights::READ, Rights(1 << 1));
+        assert_eq!(Rights::WRITE, Rights(1 << 2));
+        assert_eq!(Rights::CREATE, Rights(1 << 3));
+        assert_eq!(Rights::METADATA, Rights(1 << 4));
+        assert_eq!(Rights::EXECUTE, Rights(1 << 5));
+        // pairwise distinct: no two rights may share a bit
+        let all = [
+            Rights::LOOKUP,
+            Rights::READ,
+            Rights::WRITE,
+            Rights::CREATE,
+            Rights::METADATA,
+            Rights::EXECUTE,
+        ];
+        for (i, a) in all.iter().enumerate() {
+            for (j, b) in all.iter().enumerate() {
+                if i != j {
+                    assert!(!a.contains(*b));
+                }
+            }
+        }
+    }
 }
